# WF Clocks: the clock roster of the `clocks` Android package (org.worldfoundry.clocks).
# scripts/pack-clocks-bundle.py packs these levels, in this order, into the package's cd.iff (the
# order is the TOC index); Gradle copies this file into the flavor's assets as levels.manifest,
# where the shared LevelCatalog reads the ids and Dream labels. Add a clock here only, and only
# by appending: the index is the TOC position, and a saved Dream choice is the id.
# Format: `level <id>-standalone.iff | <menu name> [| <Dream label>]`; the id is the file name
# without -standalone.iff (wflevels/<id>-standalone.iff must exist).
# Plan: docs/plans/2026-11-21-tide-harbour-clock.md, "The bundle and the chooser" (D2 to D4)
title WF Clocks
prompt Choose a clock
level minute_machine-standalone.iff | Minute Machine | Minute Machine
level tide_harbour-standalone.iff | Tide Harbour | Tide Harbour
level cuckoo_village-standalone.iff | Cuckoo Village | Cuckoo Village
